Gotchas already mitigated in the design

- BOLT sleeps after ~5 min idle, even cradled. Two layers: every packet sets flag 0x08
  (resets_inactivity_timeout) — this is why default flags are 0x0A — plus a 20 s battery-poll heartbeat.
- noble on Windows needs an elevated terminal, and the BOLT must not be paired in Windows Bluetooth
  settings or connected to the Sphero Edu app (BLE allows exactly one central). Plus the Node 26 ABI
  issue above; doctor.js checks all of it.
- VRAM contention. Text (2.5 GB) + vision (3.2 GB) exceeds usable 6 GB, so they are never
  co-resident: unload text → vision call with short keep_alive → rewarm text. Costs 4–7 s, which is
  why LOOKING is its own LED state and the bot says "let me take a look" before swapping.
  OLLAMA_MAX_LOADED_MODELS=1. Whisper runs on CPU deliberately.
- BT speaker eats the first syllable (A2DP link wakeup). Mitigated by prepending 400 ms of silence to
  every TTS buffer. Budget ~2.5 s end-to-end response; the THINKING animation makes that gap feel intentional.
- BT speaker can steal the mic — if it exposes Hands-Free (HFP), Windows drops everything to 16 kHz
  mono. HARDWARE.md says: disable the "Hands-Free AG Audio" device, use a separate mic.
- Small models are bad at JSON. Three defenses: router.js regex-matches common commands before
  the LLM (instant and 100% reliable); the main call streams plain prose only so TTS starts on
  sentence one; a separate constrained call with Ollama's JSON-Schema format handles actions, and
  failing it degrades gracefully since the reply already happened.
- ffmpeg dshow names are exact and localized. Both camera.js and mic.js enumerate devices,
  fuzzy-match, and on failure throw an error that prints the full available device list. Also discards
  3 warmup frames — the first webcam frame is usually black.
- Charging cradle. BOLT stays connectable while charging; if packet loss appears, lift it 1 cm off
  the cradle to isolate. Noted in HARDWARE.md.

